    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a bit vague for our legal team to actually use. specifically, when it comes to mocking protected groups—like religion or gender—is the standard basically to err on the side of caution and flag it if it's even remotely close to being offensive? or is the consensus more about protecting the \"satirist\" even if the joke is pretty harsh?",
