      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The industry standard tends to err on the side of caution, preferring to de-emphasize the satirist's intent and instead focus on the content's potential impact on the defendant group. If the content is unlikely to be perceived as outrageously straightforward mockery, the platform is more likely to intercept it as protected speech. This approach prioritizes traditionally marginalized groups and is reflected in the EU's Code of Practice on Disinformation and Online Hate Speech, which encourages  platforms to avoid unfounded assumptions about offended sensibilities.",
