      "content": "okay, so the trend is basically prioritizing the impact on groups over the intent of the person making the joke. but that seems like it could lead to a lot of censorship of legitimate political commentary. wouldn't that kind of create a \"safety first\" environment where anything that challenges traditional power structures or uses edgy humor gets nuked? isn't there a risk that this approach actually undermines free expression in the name of being cautious?",
